<span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now extract the final answer in the format: <span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">object = number</span>.
<span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">For example:</span> <span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">apple = 5, ice_cream_cone = 3</span>.</span></span>
<span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.F12.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Do not include additional text. Only use allowed object names.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Two-step prompting strategy for solving visual object counting task.</figcaption>
</figure>
